  "equipment_type": "Other equipment (emergency lighting central battery system)",
  "applies_to": "CEAG CGLine+ emergency lighting central battery systems (1 to 4 lines) monitored by Eaton VisionGuard 4.0.0 or later with the BACnet/IP interface licence.",
  "summary": "VisionGuard, the PC monitoring software for CEAG emergency lighting, can act as a BACnet/IP server. For each CGLine+ system forwarded to BACnet it creates read-only Binary Inputs for the system status (failures, tests, modes) and, per line, test, mode and failure states.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet IP"
  ],
  "firmware": "VisionGuard 4.0.0 or later (BACnet/IP Interface V2.0)",
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": true,
  "notes": [
    "From the CGLine+ object table (document pages 17-19, printed in full for lines 1-4). Instances here are for a system with BACnet ID 1.",
    "Instance = system BACnet ID x 1000 + consecutive object number; the numbers have gaps as printed.",
    "Object names are printed as \"X <name>\", where X is the VisionGuard BACnet ID of the system; names are kept as printed.",
    "Line 3 and line 4 objects (consecutive numbers 88-121) only exist on 4-line systems.",
    "The guide gives no access column; all objects are Binary Inputs and listed as read-only."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "VisionGuard - BACnet/IP Interface",
    "doc_number": "V2.0",
    "revision_date": "Oct. 2020",
    "url": "https://www.eaton.com/content/dam/eaton/products/safety-security-emergency-communications/emergency-lighting/central-battery-systems/vis/visionguard/en/eaton-ceag-el-cps-visionguard-bacnet-interface.pdf"
  },
  "integration": {
    "summary": "License and enable the BACnet server in VisionGuard, forward each CGLine+ system to BACnet, then read the failure, mode and test-state inputs for the system and each line.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "BI 1035",
        "why": "Normal mode active",
        "name": "X NormalMode"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BI 1036",
        "why": "Emergency mode active",
        "name": "X Emergency Mode"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BI 1005",
        "why": "Function test active",
        "name": "X FT"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BI 1007",
        "why": "Battery duration test active",
        "name": "X DT"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BI 1001",
        "why": "Prio 1 failure (with luminaire failure)",
        "name": "X Err1"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BI 1002",
        "why": "Prio 2 failure (without luminaire failure)",
        "name": "X Err2"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BI 1033",
        "why": "Luminaire failure",
        "name": "X Lum"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BI 1048",
        "why": "Battery failure",
        "name": "X Battery failure"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BI 1047",
        "why": "Internal communication failure",
        "name": "X Communication Failure intern"
      }
    ],
    "enable": null,
    "heartbeat": null,
    "remote_sensors": null,
    "setup": [
      "VisionGuard runs the BACnet/IP server on the VisionGuard PC; it needs a licence key, and the BACnet submenu shows BACNET LICENSED and BACNET INTERFACE IN OPERATION in green when active.",
      "Server settings: device instance number, the PC network card to use and the UDP port (default 47808). BACnet Secure Connect is optional.",
      "Each forwarded system gets a BACnet ID (1-500) under Administration / BMS Forwarding."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "The objects only exist for systems forwarded to BACnet in VisionGuard; instance numbers depend on the BACnet ID given to each system.",
      "CGLine+ objects need VisionGuard 4.0.0 or later."
    ]
  },
